  "id": "Compound::DB01327 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Cefazolin, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is shown to bind to Slc22a6, a member of the Slc22 family of transporters. This binding is consistent across three distinct paths, each indicating that Slc22a6 participates in different transport activities, including sodium-independent organic anion transport, inorganic anion exchange, and anion:anion antiport. These activities are all associated with the transport of anions across cellular membranes, and Slc22a11 is identified as a participant in all three activities. The cumulative evidence suggests that Cefazolin may modulate Slc22a11 through its interaction with Slc22a6, potentially influencing anion transport across cell membranes. The mechanism is supported by the shared participation of Slc22a11 in multiple anion transport pathways, which implies a functional overlap in the transport of anions by this family of transporters. The observed scores indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Cefazolin and Slc22a11, suggesting a plausible mechanistic link that warrants further investigation.",
